<!--
  Slide 03 — Headline KPIs
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from metrics.json):
    {{REL_MULTIPLIER}}        Releases-per-window multiplier (After / Before),
                              e.g., "3.2". Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.releases.multiplier".
                              Metric 9 (Releases) per AAP §0.0 metric table.
    {{REL_CONF}}              Confidence class — one of "high" | "medium" | "low"
                              (lowercase; substituted directly into the CSS class
                              "confidence-{{REL_CONF}}"). Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.releases.confidence" with
                              .lower() applied by the renderer.
    {{REL_CONF_LABEL}}        Confidence display label — "High" | "Medium" | "Low"
                              (title-case; substituted into badge text).
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.releases.confidence".
    {{VEL_MULTIPLIER}}        Flow Velocity multiplier (After / Before).
                              Metric 2 (Velocity) per AAP §0.0 metric table.
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.velocity.multiplier".
    {{VEL_CONF}}              Velocity confidence class (see {{REL_CONF}} above).
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.velocity.confidence".lower().
    {{VEL_CONF_LABEL}}        Velocity confidence display label.
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.velocity.confidence".
    {{TIME_MULTIPLIER}}       Flow Time multiplier (After / Before). Values < 1
                              mean lead time decreased; values > 1 mean lead time
                              increased. Metric 7 (Flow Time) per AAP §0.0.
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.flow_time.multiplier".
    {{TIME_CONF}}             Flow Time confidence class (see {{REL_CONF}} above).
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.flow_time.confidence".lower().
    {{TIME_CONF_LABEL}}       Flow Time confidence display label.
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"metrics.flow_time.confidence".
    {{ACTIVE_ENG}}            Active engineer count in the after period (integer).
                              "Active" = engineers with ≥1 non-merge commit in the
                              Ramp-Up or Steady-State phase, per AAP §0.8.5.
                              Sourced from
                              metrics.json:"environment.active_engineers_after".
  Required non-text visual: a kpi-grid containing four kpi-card elements
  (class="kpi-grid" / "kpi-card" / "kpi-label" / "kpi-value"). Per AAP §0.7.1
  Rule 5 verification: every <section> must contain at least one of
  <pre class="mermaid">, <i data-lucide=, <table>, or class="kpi-". The
  kpi-grid + kpi-cards on this slide satisfy that requirement.

  Authority:
    - AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates slide_03_kpis.html.tmpl).
    - AAP §0.4.2 (per-slide HTML templates for Title, Section Divider,
      Content, Closing variants — this is a Content variant).
    - AAP §0.7.1 Rule 5 (Executive Presentation — content-slide constraints:
      max 4 bullets, ≤40 body words, ≥1 non-text visual, zero emoji, no
      fenced code blocks; Blitzy brand palette via CSS custom properties in
      theme.css; reveal.js 5.1.0 / Mermaid 11.4.0 / Lucide 0.460.0 CDN-pinned).
    - AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral Tone (no "impressive",
      "significant", "excellent", "remarkable", "unfortunately", "dramatic",
      "surprising", "notable" in the body).
    - AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 3 — Confidence Transparency (every derived metric
      carries a High / Medium / Low badge; this slide surfaces all four
      headline KPIs with badges).
    - AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 4 — Internal Consistency (the same multiplier values
      appear in the Executive Summary of acceleration-report.md, the
      Acceleration Curve table, and the Traceability Matrix; render_deck.py
      and render_report.py both read from the same metrics.json source-of-truth).
    - theme.css §Phase 7 (.kpi-grid / .kpi-card / .kpi-label / .kpi-value
      styles, with brand-primary left border and Space Grotesk display
      typography on the value).
    - theme.css §Phase 8 (.confidence-high / .confidence-medium /
      .confidence-low badge styles, with Blitzy teal / amber / red backgrounds).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes all ten
      tokens above from metrics.json and writes the result into
      acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - The "×" character on each kpi-value line is the Unicode multiplier sign
      U+00D7 (MULTIPLICATION SIGN), NOT the ASCII letter x (U+0078). This is
      enforced by verify_report.py and aligns with the report's Executive
      Summary which uses the same glyph for multipliers.
    - The fourth KPI ("Active Engineers (After)") is a count, not a
      multiplier, so it has no "×" suffix and a hard-coded
      confidence-high badge — the active-engineer count is directly counted
      from git log (per AAP §0.8.5), satisfying the High-confidence rubric.

  Tone discipline (AAP §0.7.2.2 Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral):
    - Eyebrow "Executive Summary" is a structural label, not editorial framing.
    - Heading "Headline KPIs" describes the slide's role, not the result quality.
    - KPI labels ("Releases / Window", "Flow Velocity", "Flow Time",
      "Active Engineers (After)") are metric names, not value judgments.
    - The "×" symbol denotes a multiplier; no "faster", "better", "improved",
      or other editorial framing appears.
    - Confidence badges display the rubric tier verbatim ("High" / "Medium" /
      "Low"); they are descriptive, not evaluative.

  Body word count outside tokens and pure-numeric values (verifier estimate):
    Eyebrow "Executive Summary" (2) + Heading "Headline KPIs" (2)
    + KPI labels (3+2+2+3 = 10) + Confidence badge labels (4)
    ≈ 18 words, well under the Rule 5 cap of 40.

  Verification (verify_report.py asserts):
    - Exactly one top-level <section> with class="content-slide".
    - Exactly four .kpi-card divs inside one .kpi-grid (the four headline KPIs).
    - Each .kpi-card contains a .kpi-label, .kpi-value, and .confidence-* badge.
    - Each multiplier value carries the U+00D7 "×" suffix.
    - Zero emoji codepoints.
    - No <pre><code> blocks, no <li> elements, no fenced code.
    - All ten template tokens above appear unsubstituted in the template
      source and substitute to non-empty strings in the rendered HTML.
    - class="kpi-" substring present (satisfies the non-text visual gate).
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Executive Summary</span>
  <h3>Headline KPIs</h3>
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Releases / Window</span>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{REL_MULTIPLIER}}×</div>
      <span class="confidence-{{REL_CONF}}">{{REL_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Flow Velocity</span>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{VEL_MULTIPLIER}}×</div>
      <span class="confidence-{{VEL_CONF}}">{{VEL_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Flow Time</span>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{TIME_MULTIPLIER}}×</div>
      <span class="confidence-{{TIME_CONF}}">{{TIME_CONF_LABEL}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <span class="kpi-label">Active Engineers (After)</span>
      <div class="kpi-value">{{ACTIVE_ENG}}</div>
      <span class="confidence-high">High</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
